#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:2
msgid "CMP0231"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:6
msgid "MSVC permissive mode is controlled by :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:8
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` target property selects whether compiler-"
"specific language extensions are enabled. In CMake 4.5 and below, this had "
"no influence on MSVC permissive mode. CMake 4.6 and above prefer to treat "
"MSVC permissive mode as part of the compiler extensions for C++.  This "
"policy provides compatibility for projects that have not been updated to "
"expect the behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:15
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior for this policy does not add ``/permissive`` or ``/"
"permissive-`` for :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS`.  The ``NEW`` behavior for the "
"``MSVC`` compiler keeps the compiler's default permissive mode unless the "
"request needs a different one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:20
msgid ""
":prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` ``OFF`` adds ``/permissive-`` when the selected "
"standard leaves the compiler permissive. ``/std:c++98``, ``/std:c++11``, ``/"
"std:c++14`` and ``/std:c++17`` stay permissive until this flag is passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:24
msgid ""
":prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` ``ON`` adds ``/permissive`` when the selected "
"standard implies ``/permissive-``.  ``/std:c++latest`` implies it since "
"Visual Studio 2019 version 16.8, and ``/std:c++20`` and later standard modes "
"do so as well.  The flag is placed after the ``/std:`` flag so it overrides "
"that implication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:30
msgid ""
"No permissive flag is added when the compiler mode already matches. "
"Compilers older than Visual Studio 2017 have neither flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0231.rst:33
msgid ""
"This policy has no effect on C or on compilers whose id is not ``MSVC``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` "
"or :command:`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |"
"WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
